; An effect operation was registered with a silent wildcard type and
; arity -1, so neither of these was a diagnostic. Both checked clean
; at exit 0 and the process then answered:
;
;   (two 3 4 5)   exit 139, SIGSEGV
;   (two 3)       exit 0, printing a heap address - a different one on
;                 the next run
;
; The declared arrow was never missing. The parser has kept it beside
; the name since effects landed and `axiom symbols` prints it; one
; registration site took the parallel name-only vector instead.
;
; Over-application is AX3004 rather than AX3013 because it is not an
; arity question by the time it is asked: `(-> Int Int Int)` right-folds
; to `(-> Int (-> Int Int))`, so the third argument is applied to the
; `Int` the second one produced.
(effect Two
  (two :: (-> Int Int Int)))

(:: over (-> Int Int))
(fn (over n)
  (handle (two 3 4 5) (Two) (lambda (p) (lambda (q) (* p q)))))

(:: under (-> Int Int))
(fn (under n)
  (handle (two 3) (Two) (lambda (p) (lambda (q) (* p q)))))

(:: main Int)
(fn (main) 0)
